<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nalolo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nalolo is a settlement on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lozi-people">Barotse</a> floodplain of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambezi">Zambezi</a> in Western Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, south of Mongu. It is the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mulena-mukwae">Mulena Mukwae</a>, the royal princess who rules the southern part of Barotseland, with her own court and council, under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/litunga">Litunga</a>. Like the Litunga's court, the Nalolo court moves to higher ground in its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomboka">Kuomboka</a> when the plain floods.</p></div>
